Let $R$ be a commutative associative unital ring and let $V = (V^+, V^-)$ be a Jordan pair over $R$ that is split root graded by a 3-graded locally finite root system $(R_0, R_1)$. This means $V^\sigma = \bigoplus_{\alpha \in R_1^\sigma} V^\sigma_\alpha$ for $\sigma \in \{+,-\}$, the grading is compatible with the Jordan triple product $\{\cdot,\cdot,\cdot\}$, and the grading is "split" in the sense that each homogeneous component $V^\sigma_\alpha$ contains a distinguished invertible element giving rise to an $\mathfrak{sl}_2$-triple. Associated to $V$ is the Steinberg group $\mathrm{St}(V, R)$, defined by generators $x_\sigma(v)$ for $v \in V^\sigma$ subject to the relations
\begin{itemize}
  \item $x_\sigma(u+v) = x_\sigma(u) x_\sigma(v)$ for all $u, v \in V^\sigma$ and $\sigma \in \{+,-\}$;
  \item commutator relations expressing $[x_\sigma(u), x_{-\sigma}(v)]$ in terms of the quadratic operators of the Jordan pair, whenever these are well-defined.
\end{itemize}

For the elementary linear group $\mathrm{E}_n(R)$ ($n \geq 3$), van der Kallen gave a "basis-free" presentation of the Steinberg group $\mathrm{St}_n(R)$ that avoids singling out a basis of $R^n$ and instead presents the group purely in terms of pairs of vectors and covectors satisfying intrinsic compatibility relations.

Problem. Develop a generalization of van der Kallen's basis-free presentation that applies uniformly to $\mathrm{St}(V, R)$ for every split root graded Jordan pair $V$, in a way that does not depend on case-by-case analysis according to the type of the underlying 3-graded root system $(R_0, R_1)$. More precisely: produce a presentation of $\mathrm{St}(V, R)$ by generators and relations, formulated using only intrinsic Jordan-pair data of $V$ (such as the trilinear products and quadratic operators on $V^+$ and $V^-$), that simultaneously recovers the known basis-free presentations in the classical cases (linear, unitary, orthogonal, etc.) and applies uniformly to the remaining types.

